        <h1>December 3 in Music History: The 1970s Number Ones</h1>

        <p class="post-byline">By <a href="https://musicofthe70s.net/about/author/">Charlie</a> &middot; Published {{DATE_LONG}}</p>
        <p class="jump-to-list"><a class="btn-primary jump-btn" href="#december-3-list">&#9654; Jump to the playable list</a></p>


        <p class="post-intro">On December 3 in music history, a different song sat at number one in America in every year of the 1970s.</p>
        <p class="post-intro">This page takes the Billboard Hot 100 week that contains December 3 for each year from 1970 to 1979.</p>
        <p class="post-intro">Those ten songs spent {{TOTAL_WEEKS}} weeks at number one between them.</p>
        <p class="post-intro">Four of them had just arrived, and two were duets by Barbra Streisand.</p>
        <p class="post-intro">Play any of them from the table below.</p>

